      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally settled in the late 19th century, Borup began as a railroad siding for grain storage, moving northward in 1892 to better serve the Great Northern Railway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/borup_minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early businesses in Borup included grain elevators, general stores, a bank founded around 1898, and a lumber yard established circa 1900.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/borup_minnesota",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office has operated in Borup since 1896, anchoring the community’s mail and social connections.",
